---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const title = 'Drain Cleaning in Albert Lea, MN | A-1 Drain Cleaning';
const description = 'A-1 Drain Cleaning provides 24/7 drain cleaning and sewer-line service in Albert Lea, Minnesota for clogged drains, main-line blockages, sewer backups, and recurring drain problems. Call 641-530-2728.';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description} path="/service-area/albert-lea-mn/">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] py-14 text-white sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
      <div class="container">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-300">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a>
          <span class="mx-2" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <a href="/service-area/" class="hover:text-white">Areas We Serve</a>
          <span class="mx-2" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <span class="text-white">Albert Lea</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">Albert Lea, Minnesota</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-black leading-[.98] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Drain Cleaning in Albert Lea, MN</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200 sm:text-xl">A-1 Drain Cleaning provides 24/7 drain and sewer-line service in Albert Lea for clogged drains, stopped main lines, recurring blockages, and sewer backups. When several fixtures are affected together, the restriction may be farther down the drainage system than the fixture showing the symptom.</p>
        <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="call-button mt-8 inline-block rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-7 py-4 text-center text-lg font-black text-white shadow-lg hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300">24/7 service • Albert Lea • Drain cleaning • Main drain clearing • Sewer-line blockages</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea drain service</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">Drain problems are not all the same</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A slow kitchen sink, a toilet that will not clear, and wastewater coming up through a basement floor drain can point to different parts of a drainage system. The number of fixtures involved, how quickly the problem returns, and what happens when another fixture is used are useful details when A-1 assesses the call.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">One sink, tub, or shower</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A single slow fixture can have a restriction close to that fixture. Tell us whether it is slow, completely stopped, or intermittently clears.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Several fixtures at once</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">When sinks, toilets, tubs, or floor drains are affected together, the restriction may be farther down a shared drain or main line.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Sewer backup</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If wastewater is rising through a floor drain, tub, or shower, limit water use rather than repeatedly testing the line.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Common Albert Lea calls</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">When the drain problem is bigger than one fixture</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A main drain or sewer-line restriction can show up in different ways depending on the home. In a basement, wastewater may rise through the floor drain. In a home without a basement, the tub or shower may be the lowest visible fixture.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">If a toilet flush makes a tub rise, or washing-machine discharge sends water toward a floor drain, stop adding water and tell A-1 exactly what happened.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Toilet backing up into a shower or tub</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A backup that appears when another fixture is used can indicate a restriction beyond the individual fixture. Do not keep flushing to see if it clears.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Floor drain backing up</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A basement floor drain can become the visible outlet when wastewater cannot move through the drain or sewer line normally.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Recurring main drain blockage</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If the same backup returns after a line has been cleared, the recurring restriction deserves more attention than treating each episode as an isolated clog.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Slow drains throughout the house</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Multiple slow fixtures can be a warning before a complete backup. The timing and pattern of the slowdown matter.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr]">
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Main drain cleaning</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">When several plumbing fixtures back up together</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A main drain carries wastewater from multiple fixtures toward the building sewer. When that shared path becomes restricted, the symptom may appear at whichever fixture or drain is lowest or easiest for wastewater to reach.</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">That is why a homeowner may notice a toilet problem, shower backup, laundry discharge problem, or basement floor drain overflow even though the restriction is not located at that fixture.</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A-1's main drain cleaning service is designed for these larger drain problems. If the blockage is farther out in the sewer line, the service needed may be different. The important first step is identifying the pattern instead of repeatedly treating only the fixture where the water appears.</p>
          </div>
          <aside class="border border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 p-7">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Related A-1 services</h2>
            <nav class="mt-5 grid gap-3" aria-label="Related drain services">
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/main-drain-cleaning/">Main Drain Cleaning</a>
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/sewer-line-cleaning/">Sewer Line Cleaning</a>
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/sewer-backup-emergency/">Sewer Backup Emergency Service</a>
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/">Tree Roots in Sewer Lines</a>
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/basement-floor-drains/">Basement &amp; Floor Drains</a>
              <a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/">All Drain &amp; Sewer Services</a>
            </nav>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] py-14 text-white sm:py-20">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">GOT ROOTS?</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black sm:text-5xl">Tree roots can keep coming back</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200">Root intrusion is one reason a sewer-line blockage can become a recurring problem. Roots can enter joints, cracks, or other openings in underground piping and restrict the passage available for wastewater.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200">If a sewer or main drain keeps plugging after it has been cleared, tell A-1 that the problem is recurring. That history matters when deciding what type of drain or sewer service is appropriate.</p>
          <a href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/" class="mt-6 inline-block font-black text-white underline underline-offset-4">Tree Roots in Sewer Lines →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea sewer problems</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">Sewer-line problems can look like ordinary drain clogs</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A blockage in a shared drain or sewer line can initially look like a bad toilet, slow tub, or clogged floor drain. The difference is often the pattern: more than one fixture is involved, the backup happens when another fixture is used, or the same problem returns after the line has been cleared.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">For recurring or larger blockages, A-1 can determine whether the call is best handled as main drain cleaning, sewer-line cleaning, sewer backup service, or another drain service. You do not need to diagnose the line yourself before calling.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-black">Signs to take seriously</h3>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">
              <li>Several drains slow down around the same time.</li>
              <li>A toilet flush affects a tub or shower.</li>
              <li>Wastewater rises from a floor drain.</li>
              <li>The same blockage keeps returning.</li>
              <li>The problem gets worse after heavy household water use.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-black">Useful information when you call</h3>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">
              <li>Which fixture showed the first symptom.</li>
              <li>Which other fixtures are affected.</li>
              <li>Whether wastewater is visible.</li>
              <li>Whether the line has been cleared before.</li>
              <li>What happens when a toilet, sink, shower, or washer is used.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container max-w-5xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">If wastewater is backing up</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">Protect the home while you wait for service</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">1. Limit water use</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Do not keep flushing toilets or running sinks, showers, and laundry to test a line that is already backing up.</p></article>
          <article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">2. Keep people and pets away</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Avoid unnecessary contact with wastewater and keep children and pets away from contaminated areas.</p></article>
          <article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">3. Skip chemical drain opener</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Chemical products are not a substitute for clearing a backed-up main drain and can create additional hazards for anyone working on the line.</p></article>
          <article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">4. Explain the sequence</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Tell A-1 which fixture was affected first, what happened when another fixture was used, and whether the problem has happened before.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container max-w-5xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea drain cleaning FAQ</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">Questions homeowners commonly have</h2>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5">
          <details class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-xl font-black">Do I need drain cleaning if only one drain is slow?</summary><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Not every slow drain means there is a main-line problem. A single fixture can have a localized restriction. The situation changes when several fixtures are affected or the problem repeatedly returns.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-xl font-black">Why is my toilet backing up when I run another fixture?</summary><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">When using one fixture changes what happens at another, the two fixtures may share a restricted portion of the drainage system. That is useful information to give A-1 when you call.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-xl font-black">What if my main drain keeps clogging?</summary><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Recurring blockages deserve attention to the reason the restriction keeps returning. Tell A-1 how often it happens and whether the line has previously been cleared.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-xl font-black">Can A-1 help with a sewer backup in Albert Lea?</summary><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Yes. A-1 provides 24/7 drain and sewer service for Albert Lea. If wastewater is backing up, limit water use and call 641-530-2728.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
